                                "sense_id": "e6aec782-ffca-37da-a5b7-618509e413fa",
                                "text": "\"The ability of these large locomotives to run at such high speeds without pounding themselves to pieces\", my correspondent concludes, \"is a tribute to the vast improvement in the counterbalancing of American locomotives since a day in October, 1904, when one pair of the driving wheels of a Baldwin Atlantic type balanced compound lifted off the supported wheel of the St. Louis testing-plant when exerting no more than 320 h.p."
